                                <name>DSTATAR</name>
                                <description> Pointer from where hardware can fetch the destination status information, which is registered in the DSTATx register and written out to the DSTATx register location of the LLI before the start of the next block. </description>
                                <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                                <bitWidth>32</bitWidth>
